<h1>Run Dekopon on a Mac</h1>
<p>This tutorial ends with Dekopon running on an always-on Apple Silicon Mac:</p>
<ul>
<li>You and one colleague mention <code>@dekopon</code> in a private Slack channel and get a review of a GitHub pull request in the thread.</li>
<li>It reads GitHub with a fine-grained token that only the broker holds, and it can't write to GitHub.</li>
<li>It bills one OpenRouter key with a spending limit you set.</li>
<li>Two launchd services run it under separate accounts and start it at boot.</li>
</ul>
<p>Every file below comes from the <a href="{{ starter }}">Slack GitHub recipe ↗</a> and the <a href="{{ docs }}/run-on-mac.md">Mac runbook ↗</a>. If this page and GitHub disagree, GitHub is current.</p>
</header>
